From 33b89ae8660c5816e494890c1be5d1f987232599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vlad777442 <vefirst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:59:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] replicavault: vault by metadata-only rename, copy as
 fallback (zc Phase 3)

RV_VAULT_MODE (cmake, rename|copy, default rename). In rename mode a deleted
head is moved into the vault with a cross-collection OP_COLL_MOVE_RENAME when
ObjectStore::can_move_to_collection() says the store can do it without
copying (BlueStore: no shared blobs) and the PG transaction's first use of
the head is its remove (a snapshot delete clones the head first, so those
copy). Otherwise, and always in copy mode, the old copy path is used.

The rename is staged in its own Transaction but queued in the same
queue_transactions() call as the PG transaction, ahead of it, so BlueStore
applies it in the same txc and the same KV commit as the log entry and the
remove; the remove then gets ENOENT, which _txc_add_transaction tolerates.
A copy keeps its own txc queued first, as before. remove_missing_object
stages the rename into its own transaction ahead of the remove.

A renamed entry keeps the object's xattrs and gets rv.* attrs with
rv.sha256=lazy and rv.mode=rename; the data is not read. The vaulted log
line, still from the commit callback, gains mode=rename|copy and prints
omap_keys=- and sha256=lazy for renames. F1 is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GapZ5dvT4vTJ9FHbVNTeKb
